Subject: server: allow checkpoint-less partial reuse when SWA evicted nothing

For SWA models the server only allowed partial prompt reuse through a
context checkpoint, and forced full re-processing otherwise. But when
seq_pos_min == 0 the SWA cache still holds every position of the
sequence (nothing was evicted yet), so rolling back to any prefix is
sound without a checkpoint — the checkpoint matcher itself already
makes this exact exception (cur.pos_min == 0). This makes slot states
restored from --slot-save-path files actually reusable: without it, a
restored prompt shorter than the SWA window always hit the
"forcing full prompt re-processing" path because checkpoints are not
serialized into state files.

--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
@@ -2768,7 +2768,12 @@
                                     SLT_WRN(slot, "%s\n", st1.str().c_str());
                                 }
 
-                                if (pos_min >= pos_min_thold) {
+                                // pos_min == 0 means the SWA cache still holds every position of
+                                // this sequence (nothing was evicted), so partial reuse is sound
+                                // without a checkpoint — same exception the checkpoint matcher
+                                // makes below. This makes restored slot states (--slot-save-path)
+                                // reusable for prompts shorter than the SWA window.
+                                if (pos_min > 0 && pos_min >= pos_min_thold) {
                                     // search for a context checkpoint
                                     const auto it = std::find_if(
